 "notes": "Bound on the axion decay constant f_a from a Bayesian search for a nuclear-coupled ALP dephasing the GW170817 inspiral (KCL-PH-TH-2021-25). Canonical plane is 1/f_a [GeV^-1] vs m_a [eV]. The paper excludes axions with m_a<=1e-11 eV having 1.6e16<f_a<1e18 GeV at 3 sigma; equivalently 1/f_a in [1e-18, 6.25e-17] GeV^-1. Points are the vector-extracted closed boundary of the blue GW170817 region in Fig.1 (y-axis = Log10[GeV/f_a] = log10(1/f_a in GeV^-1)), traced as a closed polygon: flat top edge at ~6.6e-17 (f_a~1.6e16 GeV) and flat bottom at ~1e-18 (f_a=1e18 GeV) for small m_a, with the sampled-mass 3sigma dots rising to ~1.35e-16 near m_a~3e-12..2e-11 eV, right cutoff near m_a~2e-11 eV. Constraint is explicitly INDEPENDENT of the dark-matter assumption, so dm_density_assumed=null. Note: the paper uses m_a = sqrt(eps) m_pi f_pi/f_a rather than the QCD mass-f_a relation, but both axes here are the paper native quantities (1/f_a and m_a directly) so no convention conversion was applied. Calibration cross-checked against abstract values.",
